00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:31.230
So these are the pictures that Natsumi sent?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.730
Episode 2

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.730
Episode 2

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.730
Can you find me?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.730
Can you find me?

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.800
"I'm in one of these. {I'm not sure if this phrasing got changed in the last episode through edits, but it's important that it stays this vague.}

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.040
Can you guess which one?

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.230
Find out before anyone disappears."

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.020
That's what this message from her says.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.940
If we take this message literally,

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:46.080
it means she's transformed into one of these twelve.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.120
And until you guess which one she is,

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.400
these people will disappear one by one.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.370
Pretty much.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.380
But it doesn't look like she's specified a way for you to respond, or even a time limit.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.000
I doubt it was omitted by accident. {I suspect it was intentional.}

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.930
I suspect that she wants to leave us in the dark in order to have complete control over this game.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.020
Maybe "game" isn't quite the right word.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:16.900
After all, there's no guarantee that whoever disappears will be returned safely.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.030
Good point. Kurumi's proof of that.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.530
We can't be certain that Natsumi's just doing this to mess around.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.400
It's possible that one of these people will disappear forever...

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.040
No.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.540
Natsumi's not like that.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:37.420
As long as I guess right, I'm confident she'll safely return anyone she's captured.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.050
You sure seem to trust her a lot.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.680
Would you ever open your heart to someone who doesn't trust you, Kotori?

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.880
When'd you become such a smooth talker?

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.430
But you're right.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.500
At any rate, we should begin our investigation.{dealing with this}

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.070
Sorry, Kotori, but I can't allow you to be a part of this mission.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.840
Naturally.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.070
There's a chance that I could be Natsumi.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.640
That means you're going to have to work a lot harder, Shin.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:12.200
What do I need to do? {Tell me what to do}

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.980
For the time being,

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:18.460
make a date schedule for each of these individuals.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.500
In order to see through Natsumi's disguise,

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:27.470
you must be able to discern even the smallest inconsistencies in their behavior.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.500
Go on a date with each one of them and look for those small nuances.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.280
It doesn't feel right going on a date while doubting their identity, but...

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.730
Morning, Shido!

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.680
Sorry, am I late?

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.990
No, you're right on time.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.640
<i>It's hard to doubt this is Tohka.</i>

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.250
Is something wrong, Shido?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.670
You seem kinda down.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.980
Y-You think so?

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.880
No, I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.420
Get it together, Shin.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.430
If she is Natsumi, acting normal won't be enough to tell her apart.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.220
Let's try stirring the pot a little.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:16.730
So, Tohka.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.730
How long has it been since we last went out like this?

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:26.160
Why would you ask that?
 We went shopping together just a few days ago.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.120
Oh, right.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.490
<i>Correct. Next question...</i>

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.860
But I'm okay going out with you any time. {as much as you want.}

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:36.370
It's always fun, and really makes me happy.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.180
Tohka...

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.560
Nice try.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.140
Playing Tohka, that is.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.380
Nice try, Natsumi.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.220
Wait, don't tell me—

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.640
Shido, who is this <i>Natsumi</i>?!

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.340
Huh?

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:58.520
Whose name did you just use instead of mine?!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.150
Who exactly is this woman, Shido?!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.270
Um, I can explain...

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.320
It's a new greeting!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.460
From the south! {a south island}

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.880
It's all the rage in Japan right now!

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.420
Natsuumi this, and Natsuumi that.

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:12.780
Oh, really?

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.030
He's gotten so good at lying.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.410
He really sold it.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.290
Oh, so it's a greeting?

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.790
So what does Natsuumi actually mean?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:28.300
Something like "I love you," I guess.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.380
Really?

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:35.580
So what were you saying about me "playing Tohka?"

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:40.560
Look, Tohka! That restaurant has an all-you-can-eat lunch buffet!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.540
We have to go there!

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.040
Lunch?

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.570
I guess that's okay.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.070
Great. Let's go!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:52.320
<i>I'm talking about eating,
 but she doesn't seem too excited.</i>

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.580
<i>Normally the mere mention of food gets her going.</i>

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.760
Still no sign of her being Natsumi.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.880
What's your take?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.500
I don't think she's Natsumi. {I think she's Tohka.}

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.380
But why does she look so sad even though we're eating?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.510
What is it?

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.780
Something wrong, Shido?

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.010
Oh, nothing...

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.980
What?! She's only eating that much?

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.060
Is she not feeling well?

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.270
Impossible! She has a black hole for a stomach!

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.520
We should eat before it goes cold.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.140
Come on.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.780
Yeah... let's.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.480
<i>Is it possible? Could she actually be Natsumi?</i>

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.290
I'm stuffed.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.560
Already?!

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.620
What's wrong, Tohka?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.920
That wasn't enough, was it?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.670
It's okay. I saw on TV the other night...

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:56.460
Be careful. Guys get turned off by girls who eat more than them.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:03.430
I didn't want to "turn you off," so I...

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:08.060
I like girls who have a healthy appetite, though.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.070
Really?!

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.240
There's no doubt. This is the real Tohka.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.870
Seems like it, but we can't conclude that just yet.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:23.870
Stay with Tohka a little longer then drop her back home by 1500 hours.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.200
Your next date should be ready by then.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.880
Sold out

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.880
Be right there!

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.260
You gotta be more careful, Shidou-kun.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.840
S-Sorry.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.890
Wait, you are Yoshinon, aren't you?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:48.150
Hi, it's everybody's idol, Yoshinon!

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:54.280
Sorry Yoshino, Yoshinon just came out of nowhere and surprised me...

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.320
T-Trick or treat.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:04.460
If you don't give me a treat, I'll play a trick on you.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.120
Shidou-san, are these...

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:20.180
I'm out of candy right now.
 I didn't expect you to come here trick or treating.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.100
Sorry, hotcakes are the best I can do.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.480
I've never had hotcakes before.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.480
Really? Go ahead, dig in.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:48.120
You had that same reaction the first time you came here.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.870
Uh...

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.380
What did I make for you back then?

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.380
It was...

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.480
You made me an oyakodon. {egg and chicken rice bowl}

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:02.980
Oh yeah, right.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:07.600
Really? I didn't know that, Shidou-kun.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.310
You don't remember?

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:15.190
Was that back when I was trapped in Origami's house?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.690
Oh yeah, that happened, didn't it?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.740
I infiltrated her house to get you back.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.330
But...

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.200
Don't worry about it. Come on.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:30.080
Shidou-san, here you go.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.960
Oh, you don't need to share. I made it for you.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.720
Okay, okay. I'll have some.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.470
Say "ahh"!

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:45.220
A-Ahh...

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.700
Does it taste good?

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.730
Yeah, it's great.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.040
Shidou-san, some syrup...

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.730
Do I have some on me?

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:08.000
H-Hotcakes don't exactly count as a treat,

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:11.370
so that was... a trick!

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:15.960
Look at you go, Yoshino!

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:20.520
Reine-san, that was the real Yoshino, right?

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:22.760
Who can truly say?

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.380
Well, who's next on the date list?

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.890
It's Tonomachi Hiroto.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:36.040
Tohka, Yoshino, and now Tonomachi Hiroto.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:40.900
It doesn't seem like any of them have any inconsistencies in their memories.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:45.560
I don't think what I just did with
 Tonomachi counts as a date, though.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:47.910
Shin, the next date is your last one for the day.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:51.820
Yuzuru's waiting for you{at the meeting place}.

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:52.910
On my way.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:55.420
Sorry Yuzuru!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.160
Anger:

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.200
You have some nerve being late to a date that you arranged yourself.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.670
Sorry, I was delayed.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:07.380
Pardon: I forgive you.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:11.840
Since I am so benevolent,
 I will allow you a five minute margin of error.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.240
Am I not enough for you by myself?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.860
No, not at all!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.990
I just felt like this doesn't happen too often.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:31.720
Rebuttal: You need not force
 yourself to deny my comment.

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:34.290
Kaguya and myself are one and the same.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:41.050
If anything, your reaction shows just how closely tied the two of us are.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:45.800
Question:

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.960
Why did you ask me out all of a sudden?

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.930
Especially at this time of night.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:55.400
Well, I thought it might be nice for just the two of us to talk.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:57.660
Do you mind?

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.960
Denial: I do not mind.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.320
But if that's the case...

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:07.820
Y-Yuzuru?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:12.740
Monopolization: Just for tonight, you are mine.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:13.990
Isn't that right?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.000
Proposal:

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.920
Would you like to go for a walk?

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:28.260
Bewilderment:

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.140
It's beautiful.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:32.010
Yeah, it really is.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.080
Clarification:

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:44.780
When a girl describes something as beautiful,
 the guy should say "but you're more beautiful."

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.980
Really?

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:49.780
Affirmation: Really.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.780
You're more beautiful.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:57.460
Smiling: Do you mean it?

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:01.040
Appeal:

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:02.980
Shidou?

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.520
What is it?

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:07.540
Question:

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:12.180
Who do you like more. Me or Kaguya?

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:16.270
I can't just pick between the two of you on the spot like this.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.020
Both of you are important to me.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.940
Scorn: Good grief.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:25.270
You chose the most cowardly answer.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.700
Give me a break.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.900
How am I supposed to answer that right now?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.600
Confirmation:

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:35.400
If I gave you more time, would you be able to come up with an answer?

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.040
Then tell me. Who do you want me to choose?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.300
Answer:

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:51.120
I will praise you for choosing Kaguya.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.760
If you choose me, I will be angry.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.310
Got it...

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:58.520
Addendum:

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.060
But if you choose me, I'll also be happy.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.820
So who's the right choice?

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.980
Sighing: I just told you.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:15.880
I wouldn't mind either way.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:20.000
That's why I'm so disappointed by your cowardly answer, Shidou.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.400
You're a chicken.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.280
However...

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:26.840
Petition:

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.360
If... hypothetically...

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:34.400
If Kaguya comes to you with the same question that I asked you tonight,

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:38.350
make sure you tell her that you'd choose her.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:40.600
Prediction:

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.100
I'm sure that Kaguya will get angry.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.840
"Why wouldn't you choose Yuzuru?!" she'll ask.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:49.580
But I'm sure that deep down, she'll be overjoyed.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.280
Yuzuru...

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.360
Confidence:

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:57.360
Kaguya may not show it,
 but she truly cares about you, Shidou.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.120
It has to be true if I believe so.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.640
Anything I hate, Kaguya hates as well.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:04.620
Similarly,

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:08.280
anything I love, Kaguya loves as well!

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:14.620
Careless: I said too much.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:18.100
I will retreat before I let anything else slip.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.850
Y-Yuzuru...

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:22.920
Petition: I'm not lying.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:25.780
Kaguya really does like you, Shidou.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:29.860
So please take care of her!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.980
W-Wait, Yuzuru!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.110
Yuzuru!

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.620
And you just let her go? {https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=59Zvv4Y9ojg}

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:50.130
I can't say I really approve of your decision to let a girl walk home by herself at night.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.120
Sorry, it all just happened so fast.

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:55.360
You couldn't help it.{There was nothing you could do}

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:58.510
Shin did a good job today.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:00.580
I know that.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:05.360
Going on four separate dates in one day isn't easy.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.730
So? What do you think?

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:10.220
You went out with Yoshino,
 Tonomachi, Tohka, and Yuzuru.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:13.980
From your perspective, did any of them seem like they were Natsumi?

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:17.620
I can't say for sure yet.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:20.370
I want to believe that none of them are, though.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:23.620
Well, I guess this wouldn't be much of a challenge if you could figure it out so easily.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:28.170
The Fraxinus scanned for unusual signs,
 but nothing came up.

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:33.220
We can't conclude anything without seeing the results of tomorrow's dates.

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.300
At any rate, go to bed already.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.930
Make sure you get enough sleep.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:44.580
Nobody will be happy if their dates with you tomorrow are messed up.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.920
I know.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:48.810
My first date's at ten tomorrow, right Reine-san?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:52.460
Yes. Your first date is with Kotori.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.320
Ah, I see why you{told him to}—

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:58.320
No! I was just telling him as the captain—

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.820
What are you still doing here?!

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:01.160
Go to bed already!

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:07.640
Arrival: I am home.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:08.710
Yuzuru?

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:11.460
What was it that you had to do?

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:15.670
Trivial: It was nothing important.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.420
Time's up.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:31.480
Haniel.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.530
That's one gone.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:41.260
Can you find me before anyone else disappears?

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:54.660
Who could it be? It's so early.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:55.640
Shidou!

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:57.170
K-Kaguya?

00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:02.380
I woke up this morning and couldn't find Yuzuru anywhere! {idk if i should time that first inaino}

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:13.940
How's Kaguya doing?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.730
Better than this morning.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:19.300
I asked Tohka and Yoshino to stay with her, just in case.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.070
I think she'll be okay.

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:32.180
Let's tell her that Yuzuru was taken aboard the Fraxinus for an emergency medical exam.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:37.130
But if Kaguya is Natsumi in disguise, it'll be a pointless lie.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.560
So how did Yuzuru disappear?

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.260
Was it really Natsumi?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.100
Yeah. Look at this.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:48.380
Is this...

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:50.700
It's footage from our unmanned cameras.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:55.820
They're filming Natsumi's targets every minute of the day.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:58.650
This is footage from right
 before midnight.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.600
Nothing strange yet.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.070
It's coming.

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.120
That's Natsumi's...

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:11.840
Yuzuru!

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:15.500
It's just as you saw.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:19.380
Yuzuru was spirited away{kidnapped} by Natsumi's Angel.

00:21:19.760 --> 00:21:24.980
I believe the person she's impersonating was taken by the same means.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:30.140
Natsumi, why are you doing this?

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.860
We can figure out her motivations later.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:36.270
We need to work hard to make sure there are no further casualties.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.540
I trust Natsumi.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:40.880
This is just a game to her.

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:43.940
And that's exactly why I'll make sure to win.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:47.160
I'll make sure nobody else disappears.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.950
That's right Shidou.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:51.450
We don't have a moment to waste.

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:54.700
Let's begin our date.

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.710
<i>But in the following days,</i>

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:01.520
<i>I learned just how powerless I was.</i>

